{
  "manufacturer": "Janitza",
  "manufacturer_slug": "janitza",
  "model": "UMG 508 power analyser (Modbus RTU / Modbus TCP)",
  "model_slug": "umg-508",
  "short_model": "UMG 508",
  "aliases": [
    "UMG508",
    "UMG 508",
    "Janitza UMG508"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power meter (power analyser)",
  "applies_to": "UMG 508 power analyser from firmware release 2.x, per Modbus address list 1.042.008.9.b (08/2022).",
  "summary": "The UMG 508 is a panel-mount power analyser with four voltage and four current channels, an RS485 port and Ethernet. It is a Modbus RTU slave on RS485 (when that port is set to Modbus Slave) and serves Modbus/TCP on Ethernet. Values are big-endian 32-bit floats that include the CT/VT ratios. This map covers the 19000-19120 'frequently required readings' block, power factor, all-tariff and per-rate energy totals, digital I/O, pulse counters and reset commands.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 115200,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are printed as protocol addresses and sent unchanged: 19000 is requested as 19000. The list starts at address 0 (real-time clock), which only fits 0-based numbering. In a 1-based or Modicon tool enter 19001 / 419001."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "2.x",
  "source": {
    "title": "Power Analyser UMG 508 - Modbus-address and Formulary (from firmware release 2.x)",
    "doc_number": "1.042.008.9.b",
    "revision_date": "2022-08",
    "url": "https://www.janitza.com/files/download/manuals/current/UMG508/janitza-mal-umg508-en.pdf",
    "pages": "Functions p. 4; transfer parameters, byte sequence, number formats p. 5; frequently required readings p. 12; date/time p. 13; other values pp. 24-26; energy pp. 27-28"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Byte order: the list says its addresses return data big-endian (ABCD for floats and 32-bit integers). Adding 32768 to an address returns the same value little-endian; that block is not listed.",
    "Transfer parameters (p. 5): 9.6-921.6 kbps, 8 data bits, no parity, the UMG 508 sends 2 stop bits (the master may use 1 or 2).",
    "Defaults for the RS485 port come from the UMG 508 user manual (https://www.janitza.com/files/download/manuals/current/UMG508/janitza-bhb-umg508-en.pdf, RS485 settings): device address 1, 115.2 kbps, and the protocol is factory-set to Modbus Master/Gateway, not Modbus Slave.",
    "The Modbus/TCP port number is not given in the address list or user manual; 502 is the Modbus default but is left blank here.",
    "Data types: short = signed 16-bit, int = signed 32-bit, uint = unsigned 32-bit, float = IEEE 754 32-bit.",
    "19068 is consumed energy of rate 1 only (its designation says HT = rate 1). For the all-rate consumed and delivered totals use 9929 and 9941.",
    "Left out: the CT/VT ratio arrays 10131-10161 (each element is labelled 'L1, L2, L3', so which element maps to which input is not clear), RS485 mode and baud (10283/10285, no value coding given), IP address/mask/gateway as packed integers, string settings, internal-use registers, harmonics and min/max/mean blocks."
  ],
